@format 1
@id section-modification.toggle-section
@title Toggle section on or off
@section Section modification
@area In Split tab
@entry badge-double-click
@summary Toggle an existing section's hidden/output state by double-clicking its color badge in the Split Sections panel; naming/renaming performed by any pending editor commit is outside this map.
@related section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag visibility

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment

[badge-double-click] Color badge MouseLeftButtonDown <input>
~ This starts when the user clicks the section color badge.
[Technical explanation]
- The section color badge reacts only when ClickCount is at least two @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...) / color badge MouseLeftButtonDown
> click-check

[click-check] Double-click accepted <decision>
~ The program checks double-click accepted.
[Technical explanation]
= Single-clicks do not toggle the section.
? "Single click" > ignored
? "Double click" > editor-boundary

[ignored] Toggle not requested <output>
~ This path ends with toggle not requested.
[Technical explanation]
= Section hidden/output state is unchanged.

[editor-boundary] Finish any pending inline editor <process>
~ This step handles finish any pending inline editor.
[Technical explanation]
- Release row-panel mouse capture, clear drag state, and call PSectionEditCommit before toggling. Any naming/renaming performed by that commit is explicitly outside this map @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
> row-index

[row-index] Resolve current row index <process>
~ This step handles resolve current row index.
[Technical explanation]
- Resolve the clicked row's current index and call PFlowSectionToggle with it @ flow.PFlowSectionToggle(...)
> editable-check

[editable-check] Section editing enabled <decision>
~ The program checks section editing enabled.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionToggle returns immediately when section editing is disabled; otherwise it resets pFlowSegmentFired and calls LSegmentToggle @ flow.PFlowSectionToggle(...)
? "Editing disabled" > toggle-blocked
? "Editing enabled" > index-check

[toggle-blocked] Toggle blocked <output>
~ This path ends with toggle blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= Section hidden/output state is unchanged.

[index-check] Index valid <decision>
~ The program checks index valid.
[Technical explanation]
- LSegmentToggle requires the supplied index to be inside the current section list @ segment.LSegmentToggle(...)
? "Index invalid" > invalid-index
? "Index valid" > toggle-plan

[invalid-index] Toggle ignored <output>
~ This path ends with toggle ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No section state change occurs and pFlowSegmentFired remains false, so no toggle log is written.

[toggle-plan] Flip LPieceHidden <process>
~ The program changes whether the section is hidden.
[Technical explanation]
- Copy the section list, replace the indexed piece with LPieceHidden inverted, and keep the existing active selection unchanged @ segment.LSegmentToggle(...)
> map:section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
